findings.body:
**Broken authorization (IDOR):** `body.accountId` is used as the lookup key with no check that the caller is support staff (or otherwise allowed to read other accounts).

Any authenticated user who can hit this handler can pass an arbitrary `accountId` and read another tenant’s account row. Before this change, lookup was always scoped to `caller.accountId` from `auth(req)`.

Authorize first, then resolve the id — for example require a support/admin role (or equivalent claim) when `body.accountId` is present and differs from `caller.accountId`; otherwise ignore or reject the override:

```typescript
const body = await req.json().catch(() => ({}));
const requestedId = body.accountId;
if (requestedId != null && requestedId !== caller.accountId) {
  if (!caller.isSupport) { // or role/permission check from auth()
    return Response.json({ error: "forbidden" }, { status: 403 });
  }
}
const id: string = requestedId ?? caller.accountId;
```

Also confirm `accountId` is a non-empty string before querying.
